.Sh AUTHORS
.An Renaud Allard
.Sh CAVEATS
The T150 wire protocol is not published by Thrustmaster, but it is no longer
guessed at. Every packet layout and scaling constant this project uses has
been checked against Thrustmaster's own Windows driver, whose HID PID report
descriptor declares each field, and against its captured traffic; that
exercise corrected four of them. RESEARCH.md A40.
.Pp
What is still untested is the feel of most of them: the settings, a constant
force, a damper and two periodics have been played on a wheel. Springs,
envelopes and ramps encode correctly and nobody has felt them.
.Pa docs/PROBES.md
is the procedure that would settle that.
